      "content": "HTML and CSS are Linked"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "You have been using our code editor, which includes two tabs—index.html for HTML and style.css for CSS—until now."
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "alt": "Tabs for Editor",
      "src": "data:image/png;base64,"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Notice how the two files work together; the CSS code you write automatically styles the HTML elements. That's because our code editor automatically links style.css with index.html."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "However, when building real-world projects, you need to manually link CSS with HTML for them to work."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Let's learn how to do that on the next page."
    },
    {
